{"type":"tool_result","run_id":"run_9d499a7a3f49","seq":17,"ts":"2026-10-30T11:44:51.382088Z","data":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-27b1408e4ff34ed58d1debcd535f51f6","name":"describe_phenotype","ok":true,"error":null,"evidence_id":"e4","kind":"phenotype","summary":"Microscopist on 4 field(s): density lower vs DMSO; 5 observations; candidates: Microtubule stabilizers","image_ids":["f_136d4ffe180f.composite","f_606ce44cd339.composite","f_cf9419af7f2b.composite","f_2abe60ff3586.composite","f_b165a4caad77.composite"],"data":{"field_ids":["f_136d4ffe180f","f_606ce44cd339","f_cf9419af7f2b","f_2abe60ff3586"],"dmso_field_ids":["f_b165a4caad77"],"model":"meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026","images":"composites only","report":{"cell_density":"lower","observations":[{"channel":"composite","finding":"Treated fields (f_136d4ffe180f, f_606ce44cd339 at 3uM and f_cf9419af7f2b, f_2abe60ff3586 at 0.1uM) show markedly reduced confluence vs DMSO control f_b165a4caad77 at identical contrast. Control is dense cobblestone monolayer; treated are sparse scattered cells/clusters.","agrees_with_measurements":false},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"beta-tubulin (green) is much brighter, thicker and more bundled in treated cells vs control diffuse filamentous network. Treated cells show intense green bundles, often circular/loops around nuclei or dense peripheral asters, with high spatial heterogeneity and texture. Visible in all 4 fields.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"actin","finding":"F-actin (red) shows enlarged peripheral ruffles/lamellipodia and overall brighter red signal. Cells are larger, more rounded/flattened vs control thin cortical actin.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"DNA (blue) nuclei are enlarged, irregular/lobed, less round and less solid. Frequent bi-nucleated/multinucleated cells and lobed nuclei. Small intensely stained condensed chromatin masses (appear yellow-white in composite due to overlap) adjacent/within cells, consistent with mitotic arrest. Control: uniform oval blue nuclei.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Microtubule texture shows increased contrast/granularity (coarse bundles vs fine mesh in control).","agrees_with_measurements":true}],"notable_cells":[{"field_id":"f_136d4ffe180f","x":732,"y":556,"why":"Large flattened cell with circular green microtubule bundles encircling irregular blue nuclei, prominent red peripheral actin - exemplifies stabilized tubulin phenotype"},{"field_id":"f_606ce44cd339","x":200,"y":307,"why":"Large cell with multiple irregular nuclei and intense bundled tubulin"},{"field_id":"f_136d4ffe180f","x":122,"y":771,"why":"Cluster with multiple small bright yellow condensed nuclei indicating mitotic/polyploid nuclei"}],"candidate_mechanisms":[{"moa":"Microtubule stabilizers","why":"Strong increase in tubulin intensity, variance and contrast plus mitotic/multinucleation morphology matches increased polymerization/bundling, opposite of destabilizer loss. Actin increase secondary to cell spreading. Consistent with both doses already maximal at 0.1uM."}],"uncertainty":"Only composites provided, reading stains by colour; no grayscale channels to separate bleed-through. Yellow-white condensed bodies interpreted as DNA+high tubulin overlap."}},"cost_usd":0.0217}}
